  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a module declaring a where-refinement (`type Pos = Int where positive`) is refused at the partition closure as partition_facts_miss, so the program never reaches member emission. v2.compiler.program_partition partition_closure_entry_for_node demands a facts entry for every node of v2.std.type_binder node_inferred_subtree_nodes, and the facts lookup returns Absent for a node under the where-predicate set. HARM: a legal module is refused by a stage that has no opinion about refinements, and the refusal names a partition fact rather than the declined subtree. Sibling of the declaration-binder-edge case recorded at node_inferred_subtree_nodes.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS (executed 2026-10-21 at origin/main bc21a38d56b7, claim_batch built and run in one remote dispatch, rc=1): src/v2/test/claim/emit/module_member_emission.dag a_where_refinement_emits_its_transparent_alias_on_the_production_route_holds FAILs while a_coproduct_beside_a_function_emits_both_in_source_order_holds and a_record_beside_a_function_emits_as_a_struct_holds PASS. A probe test over the same member_emission_refinement_verdict asserts MemberRefused with reason == ^partition_facts_miss and PASSES at main; with the where-predicate set edge also excluded in node_inferred_subtree_nodes (a scratch mutation, reverted) that probe FAILs, i.e. partition_facts_miss is gone and the refusal is a different, later one. CAVEAT: at main the claim file does not resolve at all under claim_batch, because member_emission_supplied_refinement calls emit_module_member without the tree and declarations arguments that gunbc#14387 added; the reproduction above stubs that one helper in a scratch copy. That second defect is separate and is reported beside this row.",
    "EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY (chain re-derivation, DESIGN.md 6b): v2.compiler.infer infer_where_predicate_set_edge declines the where-predicate set (it is a PARKED frontier whose predicate calls emit inhabitance_undecidable_where_predicate_subject_unmodelled), and the walker contract in v2.std.type_binder node_inferred_subtree_nodes says every stage asking infer for facts walks THE SAME set. The walker excludes the binder, order, match-arm-pattern and bind-key edges but not this one, because infer_where_predicate_set_edge lives in infer, which imports type_binder and so cannot be asked from the walker. The predicate must be homed beside the walker (as declaration_binder_edge was) and both stages ask it. Not an identity-key mismatch and not an unclassified alias: the transparent alias node itself has facts; the miss is under the declined predicate set. calm-badger-500's Edge.declaration work is adjacent only if it moves node_inferred_subtree_nodes or the edge label; the repair touches neither.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (typed loud refusal, partition_facts_miss). CEILING: structurally guaranteed, because infer and every walker ask one predicate, so no stage can demand facts for a subtree infer declines. NEXT TRIGGER: the shared predicate lands in v2.std.type_binder with an enrolled RED (a where-refinement module reaches emission) and the existing a_where_refinement claim as the accepted control; the parked where-clause itself is deleted with refinements (operator ruling 2026-10-02), which also dissolves this row's population. REPAIR NOT STARTED: reported to tidy-ant-251 before fixing.",
